{#- MCP servers reached with a credential the customer brings.

    Sibling of `mcp-public`. The whole difference is the channel: this one
    carries `${ customer_secrets.<NAME> }`, so each customer supplies their own
    token under that name and the gateway injects it upstream. Nothing here is
    ever the seller's key.

    That one reference is also what classifies the channel. `derive_channel_type`
    scans the config for the substring `customer_secrets.` and, with a static
    base_url, calls the channel **byok** — the type is derived, never declared,
    so there is no second place to keep in sync (unitysvc/unitysvc#1305).

    Enrollment is still required on top of the credential. A secret alone gets
    the customer nothing: `build_mcp_context` joins on an active enrollment, so
    the tools only appear once both exist. That "secrets + enroll" state is the
    one unitysvc/unitysvc#1813 is designed around.

    `details.tools` is the pinned manifest, captured from a live `tools/list`
    (tools/refresh_manifests.py, which needs a real token for these servers).
    It lives here rather than on the channel because it is catalog-facing and
    secret-free — the gateway serves `tools/list` from it without reading
    upstream_access_config, and it still answers when the upstream is down. -#}
{
  "capabilities": [
    "mcp"
  ],
  "description": {{ description | tojson }},
  "details": {
    "tools": {{ tools | tojson }}
  },
{%- if logo is defined and logo %}
  {#- Convenience field: ingest turns it into a logo document, and the uploader
      mirrors the external URL onto platform S3. -#}
  "logo": {{ logo | tojson }},
{%- endif %}
  "name": "{{ name.split('/')[-1] }}",
  "payout_price": {
    "description": "Customer-supplied credential — no seller payout",
    "percentage": "0.00",
    "type": "revenue_share"
  },
  "service_type": "mcp",
  "status": "ready",
  "tags": {{ (tags | default(['mcp'])) | tojson }},
  "time_created": "2026-08-15T00:00:00Z",
  "upstream_access_config": {
    "{{ namespace }}": {
      "access_method": "mcp",
      {#- The customer's own token. Resolved per call against the calling
          customer's secrets — the catalog only ever stores this reference,
          and the rendered value never reaches the context response. -#}
      "api_key": "${ customer_secrets.{{ secret_name }} }",
      "auth_mode": "customer_token",
      "base_url": "{{ upstream_url }}",
      "timeout_ms": {{ timeout_ms | default(30000) }},
      "transport": "streamable_http"
    }
  }
}
